---
import Window from "../product/Window.astro"
import CopyCommand from "../site/CopyCommand.astro"
import PreReleaseNote from "../site/PreReleaseNote.astro"
import { INSTALL_COMMAND } from "../../lib/site-facts"
---

<Window title="Quick start" lights={false}>
  <div class="body">
    <p class="p">
      With Docker and git. The demo runs the OpenTelemetry Astronomy Shop beside Prometheus, ClickHouse, Loki, Tempo and
      Jaeger, with one dashboard of its telemetry; <span class="mono">make demo-search</span> adds Elasticsearch and
      OpenSearch. The first start pulls about 12 GB of images, and the stack is healthy about a minute after that.
    </p>
    <div class="code"><span class="tl">git clone https://github.com/slashobserve/slashobserve</span><span class="tl">cd slashobserve &amp;&amp; make demo</span><span class="tl">open http://localhost:58080</span></div>
    <p class="p">When you want the agent, export a model key before <span class="mono">make demo</span>:</p>
    <div class="code"><span class="tl">export SLASHOBSERVE_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic</span><span class="tl">{"export SLASHOBSERVE_LLM_API_KEY=<your Anthropic API key>"}</span></div>
    <p class="p">The CLI installs with one line:</p>
    <CopyCommand command={INSTALL_COMMAND} />
    <PreReleaseNote />
  </div>
</Window>

<style>
  .body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 16px;
  }

  .p {
    font-size: 14px;
  }
</style>
